Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 22:49:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] From Claude - remove most of the subprocess calls.  The
 only remaining one is for estimating the size of xz files, has a fallback if
 xz is not available, and is not a security hole with the way it is written. 
 Addresses
 https://github.com/stanfordnlp/stanza/security/advisories/GHSA-c9h2-qmqw-qf6h
  Although it is worth pointing out that since this script will only be used
 with user controlled input files, this is only a theoretical security hole,
 and the more significant improvement is making this portable to Windows.

